Package: ytdlpwebui
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: systemd, python3, ffmpeg
Recommends: python3-requests, python3-certifi, ca-certificates
Section: video
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/marcopiovanello/yt-dlp-web-ui
Description: yt-dlp Web UI - web interface for the yt-dlp downloader
 A self-hosted web UI and RPC server for yt-dlp: paste a video URL,
 pick or auto-select the best quality, and the NAS downloads it in the
 background with a live progress view and a download queue. Lists,
 searches and serves the finished files from the browser, and can be
 reached from any device on your LAN.
 .
 This package bundles the yt-dlp Python zipapp and the quickjs-ng
 JavaScript runtime (required by yt-dlp to solve YouTube player
 challenges); both are built from public sources. ffmpeg is used from
 the TOS system packages for stream merging.
 .
 The web UI opens in a new browser tab via the TOS App Center route
 /ytdlpwebui/. The backend listens on loopback only: no external port
 is exposed, and all traffic goes through the TOS web server.
 Downloads, the queue database and logs are stored in
 /var/lib/ytdlpwebui; 'apt remove' keeps them, 'apt purge' deletes them.
 .
 Upstream: https://github.com/marcopiovanello/yt-dlp-web-ui (GPL-3.0)
 Upstream author: marcopiovanello. Packaged for TOS by the deb Maintainer.
